Carafe: a thread inside a system call that blocks in a Horizon wait marks itself blocked, and the server holds
such a thread when it is suspended: its registers are published at once and the wait goes on. A suspended thread
that reaches the end of its call holds itself there until it is resumed, and takes any registers set meanwhile.
Every change of the hold is signalled on its word, so the server waits for the thread instead of polling it.
LGPL-2.1-or-later, as the file it changes.

